From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000197 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: add disabled MT6797 protected clock readback

The historical MT6797 CPU clock path protects LL/L/CCI register reads and
writes with a CSPM hardware semaphore shared by the kernel, SPM, and ATF.
Expose the smallest real mainline transport for that boundary: a disabled
platform resource contract and a bounded, read-only clock-window read helper.

The helper enables only the documented CSPM internal clock, acquires the
documented semaphore with the bounded 2 ms loop, reads raw LL/L/CCI and
divider words, and requires a bounded release. A timeout or release failure
becomes sticky; no inverse is guessed. It never writes a CPU PLL, divider,
regulator, SRAM-LDO, secure register, or firmware location, and it does not
register a DVFSP state owner or clock provider. The B-cluster BigiDVFS path
and calibrated OPP state remain separate gates.

The DT node is disabled and the compile-only profile does not enable it. This
is an experiment-only transport and is not submission-ready.
